From 29e9c8b559f7288330e20f4033210308eed3e585 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:54:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: nxp-nci: Fix deadlock on driver removal while the device
 is up

nxp_nci_remove() holds info->info_lock across nci_unregister_device().
When the NFC device is up at removal time (NCI_UP set - e.g. a reader is
in use), nci_unregister_device() -> nci_close_device() calls
ndev->ops->close(), i.e. nxp_nci_close(), which takes info->info_lock
again. The mutex is not recursive, so the removing task deadlocks on
itself:

  nxp_nci_i2c_remove -> nxp_nci_remove [holds info_lock]
    -> nci_unregister_device -> nci_close_device
      -> nxp_nci_close -> mutex_lock(&info->info_lock)   <-- blocks

This hangs rmmod, driver unbind, and - because the device is torn down
with NFC still up - system shutdown/reboot.

info_lock only needs to serialize the mode change against open/close/
send; it does not protect nci_unregister_device (which reaches back into
nxp_nci_close, a lock user in its own right). The registration side
already calls nci_register_device() without the lock. Drop the lock
before unregistering, matching that.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
index 8e84beea168d..8dfd0d9eb6fa 100644
--- a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
@@ -333,10 +333,10 @@ void nxp_nci_remove(struct nci_dev *ndev)
 	if (info->phy_ops->set_mode)
 		info->phy_ops->set_mode(info->phy_id, NXP_NCI_MODE_COLD);
 
+	mutex_unlock(&info->info_lock);
+
 	nci_unregister_device(ndev);
 	nci_free_device(ndev);
-
-	mutex_unlock(&info->info_lock);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(nxp_nci_remove);
 
-- 
2.43.0

